728. Self Dividing Numbers

LeetCode Link:
https://leetcode.com/problems/self-dividing-numbers/

📌 Problem Statement

A self-dividing number is a number that:

Is divisible by every digit it contains.

Does NOT contain the digit 0.

Given two integers left and right, return all self-dividing numbers in the range [left, right].

🧠 Intuition

For each number in the range:

Extract digits one by one.

If any digit is 0 → reject.

If the number is not divisible by a digit → reject.

If all digits divide the number → add it to result.

Key idea:

Whenever a problem involves digits, always use:
digit = num % 10
num = num / 10

✅ Algorithm
For each number i from left to right:

Copy it into temp

While temp > 0

Extract digit = temp % 10

If digit == 0 → return false

If i % digit != 0 → return false

temp = temp / 10

CODE 
class Solution {

    public List<Integer> selfDividingNumbers(int left, int right) {
        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = left; i <= right; i++) {
            if (isSelfDividing(i)) {
                result.add(i);
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    private boolean isSelfDividing(int num) {
        int temp = num;

        while (temp > 0) {
            int digit = temp % 10;

            if (digit == 0 || num % digit != 0) {
                return false;
            }

            temp /= 10;
        }

        return true;
    }
}
If loop finishes → number is valid
